<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antiochus XIII Asiaticus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 64 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antiochus XIII Asiaticus was the last king of the Seleucid dynasty, son of Antiochus X and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-selene-ii">Cleopatra Selene</a>. After the Roman general Lucullus drove Tigranes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 69 BCE, he was recognised as king, but his rule was weak and contested. In 64 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> deposed him and made Syria a Roman province, and he was soon killed by an Arab ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Emesa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antiochus-xiii-asiaticus.jpg" alt="Antiochus XIII Asiaticus" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antiochos_XIII_Asiatikos,_Tetradrachm,_69-64_BC,_HGC_9-1340.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
